Package: bluerig
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: bluerig-lua
Suggests: libx11-6, libaspell15 | libhunspell-1.7-0, universal-ctags, libpq5
Description: terminal IDE, a continuation of cooledit
 bluerig is a terminal IDE that continues cooledit by Paul Sheer.  Its editor
 has syntax highlighting, code folding, an undo history browser, keyboard
 macros, a user menu, multiple windows, skins and editable key bindings, and
 works with language servers for completion, documentation and diagnostics.
 .
 bluerig -D opens the project of a directory: its tree, its build with
 meson, cmake or make, and its debugger, gdb or a debug adapter.
 bluerig -G opens a Git window on a work tree, and bluerig -Q runs the
 queries of a file in PostgreSQL, by libpq, or in MongoDB, by mongosh.
 .
 Spell checking uses aspell or hunspell, whichever is installed; libpq and
 the spell checker are loaded at run time.
 .
 The bluerig-lua package adds the Lua runtime, which runs editor scripts.

Package: bluerig-lua
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         bluerig (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Lua runtime and scripts for bluerig
 The Lua runtime plugin that bluerig loads at run time, and the editor
 scripts that come with it, such as inserting the date and time, sorting
 the selection, formatting a paragraph, drawing a table or inserting the
 output of a command.
 .
 Without this package bluerig runs, and the features written in Lua are
 absent.
